  "note": "Q4-1 spec-v2 4.2 relief zone 9 (FogRelief = FOG_MIST, MI_TD_FluidFog_Sim, same live volume path as 7A/8A). Every variant: tuning_reload reset reinit + fixed game time 8 s after reinit (L-editor-46), FogRelief forced awake and explicitly shown/hidden (order independent), others asleep, EV 0 bias, volumetric grid 8/128 and r.TDFogScattering 1 pinned like q4_fog_identity. off = tuning copy with Kinds.FogMist.TDFluidVolumeDriverSettings.bFogFloorFollowsTerrain=false; allgeom = copy with Kinds.FogMist.TDFluidTerrainHeightSettings.SceneCaptureContent=AllGeometry. Make both copies AFTER the C++ fields are built (fluid_tuning_patch checks copies against headers): python -B Tools/FluidFX/fluid_tuning_patch.py variant --out-dir Saved/AgentOps/20261110/fog-terrain/tuning/follow_off --set Kinds.FogMist.TDFluidVolumeDriverSettings.bFogFloorFollowsTerrain=false ; python -B Tools/FluidFX/fluid_tuning_patch.py variant --out-dir Saved/AgentOps/20261110/fog-terrain/tuning/allgeom --set 'Kinds.FogMist.TDFluidTerrainHeightSettings.SceneCaptureContent=\"AllGeometry\"'. Views: side = pawn (9300, 53400) looking north +Y pitch -8 (hill silhouettes against the void, flat band in front); gamecam = same pawn pitch -45 (before/after only); overhang = pawn (9300, 56300) looking west pitch -4: deviation from the spec common pawn, because from (9300, 53400) ReliefHillLow blocks the low view under the plate and a north view would put terrain-following fog on ReliefHillLow behind the opening; from the east the opening shows only flat floor and void, and the near pillar hides the far one. Run (PowerShell): python -B Tools/FluidFX/pie_lookdev_hires.py --shot-size 1920x1080 --variants Tools/FluidFX/quality/q4_fog_relief.json --fresh-pie --stop-pie --level /Game/FluidFX/Maps/LV_TDFluidFogStage --output-dir Saved/AgentOps/20261110/fog-terrain/relief/<run>. Judge: python -B Tools/FluidFX/measure_fog_terrain_follow.py regions (hidden only, check overlay) then judge --shots <run> --prereg Saved/